In the *level* file, i.e. one of the files that gets left behind
after a crash, this is the basic order of the information. I'm not
sure what all of this is, since everything I was interested in was in
the object chain.

fruit chain // presumably more than just actual fruit, since object
             // chain has those.
header/sanity checks
stairs, etc
timers
light sources
monsters
worms
traps
objects
engravings
damage
regions //shops, maybe?

So depending on where the corruption happens in the level file, the
level file might be fixable.  But if the corruption isn't detected
until the entire savefile has been compiled from the original level
files, then the information after the corrupted point is *everything*
on every level after the corrupted one.  And even if most of it isn't
corrupted, there's no way that I can see to tell what parts are
corrupt and what parts are valid.

Information about the character's stats and the game as a whole are
stored in level file #0, I believe. I'm not sure where that ends up
in the savefile, though.


